cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss PhoLine / PhO Token Wire, please cite Christian Heinrich Hohlfeld."
title: "PhoLine — PhO Token Wire: Bilingual Pre-Tokenizer Channel Compression for LLM Web Chats"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Hohlfeld"
    given-names: "Christian Heinrich"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6634-9045"
website: "https://christianhohlfeld.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChristianHohlfeld/PhO-Token-Wire"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-09-13"
abstract: >-
  Chrome Manifest V3 research prototype derived from Christian Heinrich Hohlfeld's
  PhO-Compress work. PhoLine observes normal German or English input, constructs a
  reduced tokenizer-aware channel, measures it against the original, and when it is
  cheaper replaces the matching page-level fetch, XHR, or WebSocket request payload
  before transmission. Optional paragraph-mark response atoms are expanded locally.
keywords:
  - LLM
  - token compression
  - channel compression
  - phonetic compression
  - browser extension
  - PhO-Compress
  - PhoLine
